1
00:00:34,742 --> 00:00:36,619
- Hello.
- "Hey, boy wonder."

2
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:38,746
"Guess what I'm holding in my hand."

3
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,457
- Danny?
- "The one and only."

4
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,377
- "So how you doing?"
- Good. I'm good.

5
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:46,629
It's been a long time.

6
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:50,424
- How are you?
- Yeah. Good. Good.

7
00:00:50,841 --> 00:00:53,427
Listen, I, uh...

8
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,597
I need your help.

9
00:01:00,851 --> 00:01:02,311
"Units responding to the 187"

10
00:01:02,436 --> 00:01:04,605
"at the K-Ram building
proceed with caution."

11
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:13,823
This is unit 1. We're moving in.

12
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:38,639
Freeze! Drop it!
Drop the weapon!

13
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:43,728
Turn around.

14
00:01:45,354 --> 00:01:46,397
Hey, guys.

15
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,774
It's not what it looks like.

16
00:02:08,709 --> 00:02:11,670
No, no, no, no. Y-you're going
about it all wrong, detective.

17
00:02:11,795 --> 00:02:14,715
Y-you're coming straight out
of the gate with bad cop.

18
00:02:15,215 --> 00:02:17,551
I mean, you do a good bad cop.
You are intimidating.

19
00:02:17,676 --> 00:02:18,719
I'm not gonna--
I'm not gonna lie to you

20
00:02:18,844 --> 00:02:20,429
but now let's bring good cop out.

21
00:02:20,763 --> 00:02:23,974
He's nicer, more pleasant--
we build a rapport.

22
00:02:24,099 --> 00:02:26,101
You-- maybe you say something like
"You thirsty?"

23
00:02:26,226 --> 00:02:27,478
And I say "I'd love a cup of tea."

24
00:02:28,729 --> 00:02:30,064
{\an8}Here's another fine mess, eh?

25
00:02:30,606 --> 00:02:32,066
{\an8}They really found Jane
holding the murder weapon?

26
00:02:32,191 --> 00:02:35,027
{\an8}Yes, they did. Hightower twisted
some arms at Sac PD.

27
00:02:35,152 --> 00:02:38,739
{\an8}It's a joint investigation. We share
the sandbox but CBI is taking the lead.

28
00:02:39,907 --> 00:02:41,241
{\an8}I don't know why you're smiling.

29
00:02:41,408 --> 00:02:42,993
{\an8}Well, it's a new angle
at least, right?

30
00:02:43,118 --> 00:02:45,412
{\an8}I mean, he's never been
a murder suspect before.

31
00:02:45,996 --> 00:02:48,582
{\an8}We got an ID on the victim.
Landon Wale, 45.

32
00:02:48,749 --> 00:02:50,959
He's some real estate mogul
from San Francisco.

33
00:02:51,085 --> 00:02:52,127
{\an8}What was he doing in Sacramento?

34
00:02:52,252 --> 00:02:55,756
{\an8}Well, office is a financial brokerage--
K-Ram investments, Inc.

35
00:02:55,881 --> 00:02:57,299
{\an8}Van Pelt's trying to locate the owner.

36
00:02:57,925 --> 00:02:59,218
{\an8}What's Jane say he was doing?

37
00:02:59,843 --> 00:03:02,429
I-I was taking a walk
and--to get some air

38
00:03:02,554 --> 00:03:04,264
{\an8}and when I came by here I heard a shot

39
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:06,475
{\an8}so, uh, I came to see if I could help

40
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,352
{\an8}and that's when I discovered this man

41
00:03:09,103 --> 00:03:11,480
{\an8}lying here with the blood and--and no pulse.

42
00:03:11,605 --> 00:03:12,815
He had the gun in his hand.

43
00:03:13,607 --> 00:03:15,901
{\an8}Yes, I confess. I-I picked it up.

44
00:03:17,403 --> 00:03:18,487
I'm not good with forensics.

45
00:03:18,654 --> 00:03:20,864
No, I can vouch for that.
He is, uh, terrible.

46
00:03:21,073 --> 00:03:23,409
{\an8}You heard a gunshot and ran in to help?

47
00:03:23,617 --> 00:03:25,452
{\an8}Yes, I did. I'm no hero.

48
00:03:25,577 --> 00:03:27,913
{\an8}I just did what any person
would do in that situation.

49
00:03:28,038 --> 00:03:29,790
No one is calling you a hero.

50
00:03:31,208 --> 00:03:32,543
Really? Okay.

51
00:03:32,668 --> 00:03:35,504
Detective, how'd your guys catch this? 911?

52
00:03:35,796 --> 00:03:37,840
Yeah. Uh, an anonymous call

53
00:03:37,965 --> 00:03:40,342
said a man was murdered at this location.

54
00:03:40,968 --> 00:03:42,803
- Did you make that call, Jane?
- No.

55
00:03:43,971 --> 00:03:45,514
- Why would I do that?
- Hang on, boss.

56
00:03:46,807 --> 00:03:48,100
{\an8}This was stuck in his pocket.

57
00:03:48,976 --> 00:03:50,018
Looks like a ruby.

58
00:03:50,769 --> 00:03:51,812
A pretty nice one.

59
00:03:54,481 --> 00:03:56,442
- Cool.
- Yeah, great.

60
00:03:56,984 --> 00:03:59,695
{\an8}Detective, could you uncuff
this one now, please?

61
00:04:01,447 --> 00:04:02,614
He's still a suspect.

62
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,492
And he is not gonna leave town.
Release him into my custody.

63
00:04:05,659 --> 00:04:08,328
You know he's not good for it.
Zero connection to the victim.

64
00:04:08,954 --> 00:04:10,748
"Nada. Niente."

65
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,583
Zip.

66
00:04:13,876 --> 00:04:15,627
"Naught."
I could go on.

67
00:04:16,378 --> 00:04:19,131
I am reaching out to you, detective.
I know this man

68
00:04:19,256 --> 00:04:21,592
and I know he's telling the truth
about what happened.

69
00:04:23,051 --> 00:04:25,929
{\an8}- The truth. Now.
- Beg your pardon?

70
00:04:26,305 --> 00:04:29,308
{\an8}Talk, or I will give you back
to Detective Reece. Seriously.

71
00:04:29,683 --> 00:04:31,477
{\an8}My wife's brother called me
and asked for my help.

72
00:04:31,602 --> 00:04:33,812
{\an8}He gave me this address
and when I got here

73
00:04:33,937 --> 00:04:36,565
{\an8}I found the dead guy. I guess
he called the police on me.

74
00:04:36,857 --> 00:04:38,150
Your wife has a brother?

75
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:42,196
{\an8}- Yeah. Danny Ruskin.
- Okay. Why'd he call the cops?

76
00:04:43,363 --> 00:04:45,073
- Force my involvement.
- Why?

77
00:04:45,491 --> 00:04:46,784
Well, either he didn't kill Landon Wale

78
00:04:46,909 --> 00:04:48,327
{\an8}and he wants me to help him
catch the real killer

79
00:04:48,452 --> 00:04:50,954
{\an8}or he did kill Landon Wale and he
wants me to help him elude justice.

80
00:04:51,079 --> 00:04:53,207
- And you would do that for him?
- That's a very good question.

81
00:04:53,415 --> 00:04:54,750
You know if the County Fair's
in town?

82
00:04:59,505 --> 00:05:00,881
{\an8}Mrs. Wale, what was
your husband's connection

83
00:05:01,006 --> 00:05:02,090
to K-Ram Investments?

84
00:05:03,091 --> 00:05:04,176
{\an8}Where you found him?

85
00:05:06,261 --> 00:05:07,971
{\an8}I've never heard of it before today.

86
00:05:08,514 --> 00:05:09,681
{\an8}Me, neither and...

87
00:05:10,641 --> 00:05:12,351
{\an8}my brother and I were
business partners.

88
00:05:13,268 --> 00:05:14,311
{\an8}Real estate.

89
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,731
Landon was a good man.
Why would someone wanna hurt him?

90
00:05:18,273 --> 00:05:19,316
We'll let you know.

91
00:05:20,275 --> 00:05:21,610
And we understand
that Heather Rade is here?

92
00:05:21,985 --> 00:05:24,363
Lan's assistant?
Upstairs.

93
00:05:25,739 --> 00:05:26,782
Heather!

94
00:05:29,159 --> 00:05:30,202
Concetta, honey...

95
00:05:30,744 --> 00:05:33,080
People are bringing lots of food.
You don't need to do this.

96
00:05:33,205 --> 00:05:35,165
No, I do. I need to keep busy.

97
00:05:35,582 --> 00:05:37,584
I can't believe this is happening.

98
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:39,753
Yes, Melanie?

99
00:05:40,587 --> 00:05:43,048
- Oh. The police?
- Yes, ma'am.

100
00:05:43,382 --> 00:05:45,467
Did Mr. Wale ever speak to you
about a brokerage in Sacramento

101
00:05:45,592 --> 00:05:47,511
- called K-Ram Investments?
- Sacramento?

102
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,680
Landon has a money guy here.

103
00:05:50,639 --> 00:05:51,682
Sorry, no.

104
00:05:52,391 --> 00:05:54,351
Mrs. Wale, did your husband
ever wear jewelry?

105
00:05:55,894 --> 00:05:56,937
No.

106
00:05:59,606 --> 00:06:01,984
We, uh, found this on him.

107
00:06:02,943 --> 00:06:04,820
It's a Ruby. Half-carat.

108
00:06:14,371 --> 00:06:17,916
Oh, my God. It's gone.
Why would Landon take it?

109
00:06:19,751 --> 00:06:23,672
Landon gave me the statue
of Aphrodite on our honeymoon.

110
00:06:23,797 --> 00:06:24,882
You know, Aphrodite...

111
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:26,842
The Greek goddess of love and sexuality.
Yes, ma'am.

112
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:29,261
It had rubies along the base.

113
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:33,098
I have a photo of it
for insurance purposes here.

114
00:06:33,223 --> 00:06:34,266
How valuable is it?

115
00:06:35,017 --> 00:06:37,185
It was worth over $200,000.

116
00:06:38,186 --> 00:06:40,647
Well, you should file a claim.
Looks like the killer took it.

117
00:06:45,777 --> 00:06:47,195
- Jane.
- Yeah.

118
00:06:48,238 --> 00:06:49,907
- Okay. Thank you.
- Jane?

119
00:06:50,073 --> 00:06:51,575
County Fair starts Saturday.

120
00:06:51,783 --> 00:06:54,036
- So Danny'll be there?
- Well, no. He's not that simple

121
00:06:54,161 --> 00:06:55,954
but someone there will know where he is.

122
00:06:56,121 --> 00:06:57,831
He's a carny like you used to be?

123
00:06:57,998 --> 00:07:00,375
Uh, carny is a very
broad term, Lisbon.

124
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,794
Uh, Danny's more showbiz
but it's--it's been a while.

125
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,464
Before last night, when was
the last time you talked to him?

126
00:07:07,799 --> 00:07:10,260
When I called him to tell him
what Red John had done.

127
00:07:12,763 --> 00:07:15,974
Boss? K-Ram Investments
doesn't exist.

128
00:07:16,183 --> 00:07:17,851
It's not registered
on any stock exchange.

129
00:07:17,976 --> 00:07:19,811
- It's not even a real company.
- Who owns it?

130
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,647
A holding company
signed the lease.

131
00:07:21,772 --> 00:07:24,942
I tracked that through three other outfits
to get to a Daniel Ruskin.

132
00:07:25,442 --> 00:07:27,569
Daniel Ruskin. He got a sheet?

133
00:07:27,819 --> 00:07:32,658
Long one. Got hooked for larceny
passing bad checks. Nothing violent.

134
00:07:32,908 --> 00:07:35,243
Then was popped for fraud
two years ago in Toronto.

135
00:07:35,535 --> 00:07:37,079
He's a con man, basically.

136
00:07:38,121 --> 00:07:41,500
- Show business, eh?
- Well, confidence, game, showbiz--

137
00:07:41,917 --> 00:07:42,960
it's a thin line.

138
00:07:43,085 --> 00:07:45,921
So maybe the victim was a mark
in one of Danny's cons.

139
00:07:46,046 --> 00:07:47,756
Vic finds out. They fight.

140
00:07:47,881 --> 00:07:49,800
Danny kills him
and steals the statuette.

141
00:07:49,967 --> 00:07:52,761
Possible. Danny is usually
smoother than that.

142
00:07:53,136 --> 00:07:56,139
Right. Very smooth, the way
he forced you onto this case.

143
00:07:56,264 --> 00:07:58,684
It's clever.
You're a pawn in his game.

144
00:07:58,934 --> 00:08:00,185
I'm not a pawn. He...

145
00:08:01,311 --> 00:08:02,896
Yeah? What?

146
00:08:03,021 --> 00:08:04,815
Oh, you're very good.
You almost got me talking.

147
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,358
All right.
What are you keeping from me?

148
00:08:06,483 --> 00:08:08,443
Nothing. He's family.
That's all.

149
00:08:08,568 --> 00:08:10,237
- "Van Pelt."
- Complicated, right?

150
00:08:10,362 --> 00:08:12,197
"Boss, it's Detective Reece for you."

151
00:08:12,322 --> 00:08:13,615
- They got a call to Jane's phone
- It's for you.

152
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:16,243
- from the K-Ram offices.
- He's on his way over.

153
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:17,703
Stall him.

154
00:08:17,911 --> 00:08:18,954
Stall him?

155
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,684
I didn't know your wife
was from this world, too.

156
00:08:42,019 --> 00:08:45,439
Oh, yeah.
Her grandparents were carny royalty.

157
00:08:46,732 --> 00:08:47,816
They ran big metal--

158
00:08:48,316 --> 00:08:50,193
Ferris wheels, ghost trains.

159
00:08:50,652 --> 00:08:52,029
They ran 'em all across the Midwest

160
00:08:52,154 --> 00:08:54,281
but, uh, my wife--
she, uh...

161
00:08:55,449 --> 00:08:56,575
She didn't wanna have any part of it.

162
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,243
Why?

163
00:08:58,994 --> 00:09:00,037
Well...

164
00:09:01,121 --> 00:09:02,664
Carnies are good people
but, uh--

165
00:09:02,789 --> 00:09:04,541
you know, you're either
with the show or you're not.

166
00:09:04,666 --> 00:09:06,001
There's-- there's nowhere
in the middle.

167
00:09:06,126 --> 00:09:08,128
And if you're not with the show
then you're a mark.

168
00:09:08,754 --> 00:09:09,796
You're a sucker.

169
00:09:10,922 --> 00:09:11,965
And she didn't like that.

170
00:09:12,924 --> 00:09:15,469
You're not gonna need the badge.
They're gonna tell you're a cop without it.

171
00:09:16,303 --> 00:09:19,139
Actually, people very rarely
guess I'm a cop.

172
00:09:19,264 --> 00:09:21,058
Oh, yeah. Let me do the talking.

173
00:09:21,224 --> 00:09:22,517
When it's advisable.

174
00:09:22,934 --> 00:09:25,729
- And don't mention Danny until I do.
- I'll be the judge of that.

175
00:09:26,063 --> 00:09:27,981
Hey! No trespassing.

176
00:09:28,774 --> 00:09:30,484
Fair's not open yet.
Scram.

177
00:09:31,943 --> 00:09:32,986
Or else what?

178
00:09:36,573 --> 00:09:38,867
Or else I'll give you a good whoppin'.
That's what else.

179
00:09:39,201 --> 00:09:41,203
Uh, how about this, Pete?
If you can catch me

180
00:09:41,703 --> 00:09:44,206
then I will marry that damn
ugly sister of yours.

181
00:09:48,835 --> 00:09:51,213
Patrick Jane.
Son of a bitch.

182
00:09:54,299 --> 00:09:55,592
Oh, man!

183
00:09:58,011 --> 00:09:59,304
I heard you were police.

184
00:09:59,888 --> 00:10:01,139
I didn't believe it

185
00:10:01,556 --> 00:10:03,433
but here you are
with a real, live cop.

186
00:10:03,642 --> 00:10:05,102
This is my good friend Teresa.

187
00:10:05,769 --> 00:10:06,812
Doesn't bite.

188
00:10:07,354 --> 00:10:11,066
If you're okay with Jane
I guess you're okay with me.

189
00:10:11,608 --> 00:10:12,651
Thanks.

190
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:15,153
You know, I haven't
seen you a while, eh?

191
00:10:15,278 --> 00:10:16,321
Well, you know.

192
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:19,032
Yeah, I know.
So what brings you here now?

193
00:10:19,199 --> 00:10:21,201
- I'll give you three guesses.
- Uh, Danny?

194
00:10:21,451 --> 00:10:22,494
Got it in one.

195
00:10:23,036 --> 00:10:25,247
- Danny's a good boy.
- What's he been up to?

196
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:27,666
Hey, Sam.
Come on out here.

197
00:10:27,791 --> 00:10:29,292
I got a surprise for you, honey.

198
00:10:29,835 --> 00:10:30,877
Come on. You ready?

199
00:10:31,962 --> 00:10:33,713
Oh, look at you, huh?

200
00:10:34,965 --> 00:10:36,007
Yeah.

201
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,387
- Uh, what was that for?
- Detroit.

202
00:10:40,595 --> 00:10:42,305
Oh, yeah. Fair enough.

203
00:10:43,306 --> 00:10:44,558
What's with the State Trooper?

204
00:10:44,808 --> 00:10:48,270
Yeah, it's, like, unreal, huh?
A Jane working with the law.

205
00:10:48,770 --> 00:10:50,605
- How do I look like a cop?
- Oh, please.

206
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:53,191
Look like Cagney and Lacey
had a baby, called it Pepper.

207
00:10:54,234 --> 00:10:56,528
- They're looking for Danny.
- Danny's in trouble.

208
00:10:56,778 --> 00:10:58,989
Yeah, what else is new?
Danny's always in trouble.

209
00:10:59,239 --> 00:11:00,866
Remember the morning
of your wedding?

210
00:11:02,701 --> 00:11:07,289
Oh, yes. Yeah. My--my wife had
to bail Danny out in her dress.

211
00:11:07,414 --> 00:11:08,540
She was not very happy.

212
00:11:09,291 --> 00:11:12,377
Well, it's good to see you and all
but the police is the police. No offense.

213
00:11:12,919 --> 00:11:13,962
None taken.

214
00:11:14,546 --> 00:11:16,756
Well, Pete, wh-why don't you
take Pepper here

215
00:11:16,882 --> 00:11:18,717
and, uh, show her the elephant?

216
00:11:20,051 --> 00:11:23,430
- I'd love to see the elephant.
- My pleasure. Right this way.

217
00:11:25,473 --> 00:11:26,683
Her name is Daisy.

218
00:11:27,601 --> 00:11:28,643
She's cute.

219
00:11:29,561 --> 00:11:30,896
She's a mean old girl.

220
00:11:31,188 --> 00:11:33,023
She'd run down her own kids
for an apple.

221
00:11:33,148 --> 00:11:34,191
No.

222
00:11:34,524 --> 00:11:36,234
You think I'm kidding?
Here. Give her one.

223
00:11:36,735 --> 00:11:38,695
- Where do I put it?
- In here.

224
00:11:41,239 --> 00:11:43,158
You two get along
you can take her home with you.

225
00:11:43,658 --> 00:11:44,743
You want another one?

226
00:11:47,579 --> 00:11:48,914
What kinda trouble Danny got?

227
00:11:49,915 --> 00:11:51,166
Worst kind of trouble.

228
00:11:52,042 --> 00:11:53,126
Damn shame.

229
00:11:54,586 --> 00:11:55,712
Not surprised though.

230
00:11:56,213 --> 00:11:59,090
Danny's been heading downhill
all the way since Angela died.

231
00:11:59,841 --> 00:12:01,593
There's a man
need a big sister.

232
00:12:03,595 --> 00:12:05,263
- Yeah.
- So...

233
00:12:06,014 --> 00:12:08,975
I should help you
and the cops find him...

234
00:12:10,435 --> 00:12:11,478
Why?

235
00:12:12,812 --> 00:12:15,982
Danny called me,
uh, just out of the blue

236
00:12:16,107 --> 00:12:17,234
and he asked for my help.

237
00:12:17,567 --> 00:12:21,404
Danny doesn't always do
what's best for his own interests.

238
00:12:21,821 --> 00:12:24,908
- Tendency to outfox himself.
- True.

239
00:12:27,577 --> 00:12:29,454
But he asked for my help
and that's what I'll give him.

240
00:12:36,127 --> 00:12:38,588
A few hours ago, I was wiping
a murder weapon clean

241
00:12:38,797 --> 00:12:40,715
in case it had Danny's fingerprints
on it.

242
00:12:47,472 --> 00:12:49,432
I don't know
where Danny is now...

243
00:12:52,102 --> 00:12:53,353
But Nicki does.

244
00:12:54,604 --> 00:12:56,064
Talk to Biltmore Nicki.

245
00:12:58,775 --> 00:13:00,485
Same gig as always.

246
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:06,574
It's good to see you.

247
00:13:07,784 --> 00:13:09,411
I'm glad you're doing okay.

248
00:13:11,037 --> 00:13:12,330
You are doing okay, aren't you?

249
00:13:12,706 --> 00:13:13,748
Oh, yeah.

250
00:13:18,461 --> 00:13:21,214
My little friend Pepper is gonna need
a ride back to the office.

251
00:13:21,506 --> 00:13:22,549
She's huge.

252
00:13:25,552 --> 00:13:26,720
Kinda tickles.

253
00:13:31,308 --> 00:13:32,350
Hey!

254
00:13:34,185 --> 00:13:35,228
Jane!

255
00:13:44,794 --> 00:13:46,629
Detective Reece called three times.
He's pissed.

256
00:13:46,754 --> 00:13:48,798
He can get in line.
Where's Van Pelt?

257
00:13:49,173 --> 00:13:51,092
Oh, hey, boss.
Can I borrow the car?

258
00:13:52,385 --> 00:13:54,262
That's funny.
Anything on Ruskin?

259
00:13:54,387 --> 00:13:56,681
Uh, yeah, he's a, uh,
former escape artist.

260
00:13:56,806 --> 00:13:59,600
Had an act as a kid
just like Jane, Houdini Junior.

261
00:13:59,767 --> 00:14:01,978
Says he could do the water
torture cell trick at 17

262
00:14:02,103 --> 00:14:04,397
which I guess is good
if you like that sort of thing.

263
00:14:05,064 --> 00:14:06,607
Cho, go and talk
to the victim's wife.

264
00:14:06,732 --> 00:14:08,025
See if she knows Ruskin.

265
00:14:08,359 --> 00:14:11,070
Rigsby, have Van Pelt help you
look into his financials.

266
00:14:11,279 --> 00:14:13,698
Look for other names.
Con men rarely work alone.

267
00:14:14,157 --> 00:14:15,491
Where is Van Pelt?

268
00:14:28,754 --> 00:14:30,173
Daniel Ruskin.

269
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:33,217
I don't know him. Sorry.

270
00:14:34,594 --> 00:14:35,636
But you do?

271
00:14:37,096 --> 00:14:40,016
I have met Daniel.
He's very charming.

272
00:14:41,142 --> 00:14:43,811
- I'm sure he wouldn't hurt Landon.
- You know Ruskin?

273
00:14:45,021 --> 00:14:47,023
But you told us you never heard
of his company, K-Ram.

274
00:14:47,982 --> 00:14:52,653
No. I-I have no notion of his business.
I met Daniel socially...

275
00:14:53,362 --> 00:14:55,907
at Landon's country club--
Murphy introduced us.

276
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,366
Murphy Traver?

277
00:14:57,742 --> 00:15:01,078
Oh, a lovely man.
Of the Long Island Travers.

278
00:15:06,626 --> 00:15:08,294
Thank you for your cooperation, Mr. Traver.

279
00:15:08,419 --> 00:15:09,754
Oh, happy to talk, agents.

280
00:15:09,879 --> 00:15:11,881
Yeah, I just need to get back
to this meeting in a few.

281
00:15:12,298 --> 00:15:15,051
Can't trust computer nerds alone
too long, you know.

282
00:15:15,968 --> 00:15:18,387
Oh, gosh.
Poor Landon. It's horrible.

283
00:15:18,513 --> 00:15:19,764
So you introduced him
to Ruskin?

284
00:15:19,931 --> 00:15:22,725
Yeah, yeah. Sure did.
I, uh yeah, met Daniel at the club.

285
00:15:22,850 --> 00:15:24,310
He's just an outstanding guy.

286
00:15:24,477 --> 00:15:26,187
But, well, why do you wanna
know about Daniel?

287
00:15:26,729 --> 00:15:29,106
Well, he's a con man.
He may have killed Mr. Wale.

288
00:15:29,774 --> 00:15:32,568
- You know where he is?
- Con man? Oh, my God.

289
00:15:32,902 --> 00:15:35,279
My God. I invested with him.
Oh, my God.

290
00:15:36,572 --> 00:15:37,823
Where's your assistant?

291
00:15:39,909 --> 00:15:42,203
I'm--I'm sorry, agent.
I-I have to call my bank.

292
00:15:42,328 --> 00:15:43,955
Yeah, you know, a place like this,
bunch of people

293
00:15:44,121 --> 00:15:46,165
you should have an assistant.
At least a receptionist.

294
00:15:46,332 --> 00:15:47,625
And with all those employees

295
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:49,919
the phone lines should be
ringing off the hook.

296
00:15:50,545 --> 00:15:53,297
Landlines. So 20th-century.
No, agent. I-I'm sorry.

297
00:15:53,422 --> 00:15:55,508
You c-- you're not allowed in there.
That's a clean room, agent!

298
00:16:00,179 --> 00:16:01,347
Very clean.

299
00:16:09,772 --> 00:16:12,233
I am having a very bad day

300
00:16:13,025 --> 00:16:14,944
and you're gonna tell us
about Daniel Ruskin.

301
00:16:15,069 --> 00:16:16,904
- Come on.
- Okay. All right.

302
00:16:23,286 --> 00:16:26,080
My dear, sorry to bother.

303
00:16:26,539 --> 00:16:28,624
Did you see two boys
run down the street?

304
00:16:29,208 --> 00:16:30,251
No.

305
00:16:30,835 --> 00:16:35,089
- Ma'am, what's wrong?
- I was walking to the train station

306
00:16:35,214 --> 00:16:36,382
it's such a nice day--

307
00:16:36,549 --> 00:16:39,969
and these two boys
just took my purse.

308
00:16:40,136 --> 00:16:41,512
Ma'am, here. Come here.
Sit down.

309
00:16:46,142 --> 00:16:48,144
I have to visit my sister.

310
00:16:48,561 --> 00:16:51,147
She's in the hospital
in Bakersfield.

311
00:16:52,023 --> 00:16:54,942
- I feel so stupid.
- That's terrible.

312
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:59,530
And the--the last train to Bakersfield
leaves in 40 minutes.

313
00:17:00,072 --> 00:17:01,115
Oh, dear.

314
00:17:01,616 --> 00:17:04,118
Oh. Look, uh...

315
00:17:05,578 --> 00:17:07,830
Can I drive you
to the train station?

316
00:17:08,289 --> 00:17:09,373
You would do that?

317
00:17:09,999 --> 00:17:11,083
Oh, my dear.

318
00:17:11,542 --> 00:17:13,294
- Oh, thank you.
- Sure.

319
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,213
"You're not taking her
anywhere, Grace."

320
00:17:20,551 --> 00:17:21,802
Nice hook, Nicki.

321
00:17:24,764 --> 00:17:26,599
You're such a sweet old lady.

322
00:17:28,267 --> 00:17:29,769
Grace, Nicki. Nicki, Grace.

323
00:17:30,227 --> 00:17:33,856
If this were for real, this old fox
would have you stripped bare.

324
00:17:36,275 --> 00:17:38,986
This sweet piece of fruit
is a cop?

325
00:17:40,071 --> 00:17:41,113
Damn.

326
00:17:41,822 --> 00:17:44,659
- Guess I'm losing my touch.
- I'm looking for Danny.

327
00:17:46,452 --> 00:17:48,454
- Look at me.
- Danny?

328
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:50,873
Look at me.

329
00:17:51,415 --> 00:17:52,500
This is a family thing.

330
00:17:53,209 --> 00:17:55,086
I know you know where he is.
Tell me, Nicki

331
00:17:55,211 --> 00:17:56,879
or this nice piece of fruit
will take you downtown

332
00:17:57,004 --> 00:17:59,173
and treat you to a complimentary
cavity search.

333
00:18:04,553 --> 00:18:07,181
- Hypothetically, what happened?
- Hypothetically?

334
00:18:09,517 --> 00:18:11,602
We were running "the rag".

335
00:18:12,144 --> 00:18:14,772
"We'll let you invest
in a surefire stock market winner."

336
00:18:14,897 --> 00:18:17,900
"It's a little illegal. Don't tell anybody.
Blah, blah."

337
00:18:19,026 --> 00:18:20,069
Hypothetically...

338
00:18:21,028 --> 00:18:22,697
Danny hooked Landon good.

339
00:18:22,822 --> 00:18:24,782
I mean, had him begging us
to let him invest.

340
00:18:24,907 --> 00:18:28,077
He was bringing us
some statue worth 200 grand.

341
00:18:28,202 --> 00:18:30,204
So you and Danny killed Landon
and took the statue?

342
00:18:30,579 --> 00:18:33,374
No. No. Why take it when he was
gonna give it to us in the morning?

343
00:18:33,499 --> 00:18:34,667
Maybe you took it, Murphy.

344
00:18:35,126 --> 00:18:36,502
You didn't wanna share with Danny

345
00:18:36,627 --> 00:18:38,337
so you called Wale
and met him early.

346
00:18:38,671 --> 00:18:41,465
Things got outta hand. You need
to help yourself, tell your side.

347
00:18:41,716 --> 00:18:42,800
No, no, no, no.

348
00:18:42,925 --> 00:18:44,593
- You're a liar.
- She's right. You are.

349
00:18:44,885 --> 00:18:46,011
Where's Danny Ruskin?

350
00:18:48,806 --> 00:18:51,517
You're a businessman, so's Danny.
He'll understand.

351
00:18:52,685 --> 00:18:54,562
I don't know. I don't.

352
00:18:55,896 --> 00:18:57,356
But I know who he's with.

353
00:18:57,857 --> 00:18:59,734
Trixie... somebody.

354
00:19:00,192 --> 00:19:01,986
Rich and hot.

355
00:19:02,611 --> 00:19:05,614
Yeah. Danny's always got
a second revenue stream.

356
00:19:06,282 --> 00:19:07,324
Always...

357
00:19:07,992 --> 00:19:09,076
monetizing.

358
00:19:14,790 --> 00:19:17,293
Excuse me.
Jane, where the hell are you?

359
00:19:17,626 --> 00:19:19,211
"Wow. Hope that's the decaf
you're getting."

360
00:19:19,378 --> 00:19:21,589
- How did you--
- "I can hear the foam machine."

361
00:19:22,590 --> 00:19:24,967
Anyway, I promised Grace
I'd call, so I called.

362
00:19:25,259 --> 00:19:26,594
Lovely to talk to you. Bye now.

363
00:19:26,844 --> 00:19:28,637
- Put her on now.
- No, I've already ditched her.

364
00:19:28,763 --> 00:19:32,057
Jane, you have to come in.
Danny could be dangerous.

365
00:19:32,183 --> 00:19:34,602
We're not looking to use
deadly force, but things happen.

366
00:19:34,727 --> 00:19:35,811
It's not safe for you.

367
00:19:35,936 --> 00:19:38,397
Getting close to nabbing him, are you?
Oh, that's good to hear.

368
00:19:38,856 --> 00:19:40,441
Well, may the best man win, Lisbon.

369
00:19:40,983 --> 00:19:42,026
- Jane!
- Boss.

370
00:19:44,653 --> 00:19:47,281
Checked the sign-in logs at the K-Ram
offices. Found a Trixie Mercado.

371
00:19:47,531 --> 00:19:48,908
She's the daughter of the guy
who owns the building.

372
00:19:49,033 --> 00:19:50,659
- She has a place in Midtown.
- Thanks.

373
00:19:52,077 --> 00:19:53,496
May the best man win.

374
00:19:56,665 --> 00:19:59,668
Detective Reece, it's Lisbon.
We've got a lead on Ruskin.

375
00:20:02,004 --> 00:20:04,507
It's party time.

376
00:20:07,301 --> 00:20:08,469
Baby, why are you packing?

377
00:20:09,011 --> 00:20:11,931
God, you are killing me.
You're so gorgeous.

378
00:20:12,264 --> 00:20:15,935
Seriously, uh, I'm dying
but I gotta go, baby.

379
00:20:16,310 --> 00:20:17,353
Something came up.

380
00:20:17,853 --> 00:20:19,188
I'll be back soon, all right?

381
00:20:20,773 --> 00:20:21,941
- Danny.
- Hey.

382
00:20:22,483 --> 00:20:23,526
Long time.

383
00:20:25,361 --> 00:20:26,403
Danny, what the hell?

384
00:20:27,071 --> 00:20:28,823
You must be, uh, Trixie, huh?

385
00:20:29,657 --> 00:20:30,991
Hi. I'm--I'm Patrick.

386
00:20:31,116 --> 00:20:32,952
No need to be scared.
Danny and I--we're family.

387
00:20:33,786 --> 00:20:36,205
Biltmore Nicki called you, huh? And that's
it, you're just gonna hop on out of here?

388
00:20:36,330 --> 00:20:37,623
- I--You're mad.
- I just got here.

389
00:20:37,748 --> 00:20:39,208
You're mad. I get that. I do.

390
00:20:39,333 --> 00:20:40,960
But I needed your help.

391
00:20:41,377 --> 00:20:42,795
I needed your wisdom
and--and cunning and--

392
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:45,047
Yeah, how much help can I be to you
when I'm in handcuffs, Danny?

393
00:20:45,381 --> 00:20:46,757
Wh-what can I say?

394
00:20:47,091 --> 00:20:49,552
Calling you in was the best
of some very unsavory options.

395
00:20:49,677 --> 00:20:51,345
Then tell me what happened
with Landon Wale last night--

396
00:20:51,512 --> 00:20:53,305
honest and quick.
I don't have all day.

397
00:20:54,682 --> 00:20:55,975
"Police, open up!'

398
00:20:59,603 --> 00:21:01,689
- You son of a bitch.
- That has nothing to do with me.

399
00:21:01,814 --> 00:21:03,315
"Trixie Mercado, are you in there?"

400
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:06,068
- "We've got some questions."
- Oh, please.

401
00:21:07,236 --> 00:21:08,904
What the hell is going on?

402
00:21:10,072 --> 00:21:12,116
Look, just talk to 'em.
I have influence.

403
00:21:12,241 --> 00:21:13,993
- We can sort this thing out.
- "Ms. Mercado?"

404
00:21:14,118 --> 00:21:16,328
If you didn't do anything
you got nothing to worry about.

405
00:21:16,620 --> 00:21:17,663
Nothing to worry about?

406
00:21:17,913 --> 00:21:20,541
I am not spending a day in jail!
Not one day.

407
00:21:21,208 --> 00:21:22,877
Never again. Ever. You got me?

408
00:21:31,492 --> 00:21:33,744
Ms. Mercado, open the door
right now!

409
00:21:34,161 --> 00:21:36,205
Back up. I'm going in.
Give me some room.

410
00:21:38,165 --> 00:21:39,208
Back up!

411
00:21:44,296 --> 00:21:47,591
Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Danny's not here.

412
00:21:54,056 --> 00:21:55,098
Yep.

413
00:21:55,599 --> 00:21:56,642
Danny went that way.

414
00:21:57,643 --> 00:21:58,685
All by himself.

415
00:21:58,811 --> 00:22:01,188
All units search the area.
Suspect has fled.

416
00:22:01,313 --> 00:22:03,857
Establish a 2-block perimeter
around this block.

417
00:22:05,818 --> 00:22:07,778
Hey. You're Patrick's friend, right?

418
00:22:08,403 --> 00:22:09,446
- Yeah.
- He said to tell you

419
00:22:09,571 --> 00:22:11,406
he's really, really sorry about all this.

420
00:22:11,573 --> 00:22:12,825
Jane's with Danny?

421
00:22:13,534 --> 00:22:15,369
Jane? No.

422
00:22:15,911 --> 00:22:18,372
It was a man. Patrick.

423
00:22:24,127 --> 00:22:26,046
Tell me what happened
with Landon Wale.

424
00:22:27,130 --> 00:22:29,633
- Ooh, big detective.
- Consultant.

425
00:22:30,509 --> 00:22:31,552
Consultant.

426
00:22:31,677 --> 00:22:33,554
Stop stalling. Just tell me
if you killed the man

427
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:34,930
and I'll take you to Mexico.

428
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:37,140
I'm touched. Cabo?

429
00:22:37,766 --> 00:22:39,935
- You--you'd do that for me?
- Yes, I would.

430
00:22:40,519 --> 00:22:41,562
Why?

431
00:22:42,479 --> 00:22:44,231
Because your sister
would want me to.

432
00:22:44,606 --> 00:22:47,025
You sound like a mark.
Or you think I'm a mark.

433
00:22:47,734 --> 00:22:49,403
- Which?
- You sound like you're in over your head.

434
00:22:49,528 --> 00:22:51,196
Yeah, way over my head.

435
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:54,032
Not like Patrick. No.

436
00:22:54,324 --> 00:22:56,451
You would never get in
way over your head, would you?

437
00:22:56,618 --> 00:22:59,288
Too smart for that, never make
mistakes. Not the boy wonder.

438
00:22:59,538 --> 00:23:01,123
Why won't you answer
my question?

439
00:23:02,958 --> 00:23:04,167
Is it because you hate me?

440
00:23:04,751 --> 00:23:06,837
Or is it because you did
in fact, kill the man?

441
00:23:08,255 --> 00:23:09,298
Hate.

442
00:23:10,924 --> 00:23:12,384
Why would I hate you, bro?

443
00:23:13,010 --> 00:23:14,803
I asked my question first.

444
00:23:15,846 --> 00:23:17,180
I didn't kill Landon.

445
00:23:19,433 --> 00:23:20,851
I smell deception

446
00:23:21,602 --> 00:23:23,937
but it's hard to tell with you
because you're kind of a sociopath

447
00:23:24,062 --> 00:23:25,480
like all the great con men.

448
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,608
I am great, huh?

449
00:23:29,318 --> 00:23:31,737
First compliment you ever
gave me, I can recall.

450
00:23:32,696 --> 00:23:34,615
Convince me, Danny.
Come on. Try.

451
00:23:34,781 --> 00:23:37,409
Just--just make me believe
that you didn't kill that guy.

452
00:23:37,618 --> 00:23:42,414
You want me to dance for you?
Hmm? I should crawl for you?

453
00:23:42,623 --> 00:23:45,125
Okay, that's it. I'm leaving
and I'm gonna call the cops.

454
00:23:45,250 --> 00:23:46,710
They will be here
in five minutes.

455
00:23:47,085 --> 00:23:48,378
I'd make yourself scarce.

456
00:23:49,963 --> 00:23:51,006
Stop!

457
00:23:51,632 --> 00:23:52,674
Stop!

458
00:23:54,885 --> 00:23:56,053
You think I won't do it?

459
00:23:57,054 --> 00:23:58,096
Not sure.

460
00:23:59,890 --> 00:24:02,517
But... I wouldn't blame you
if you did.

461
00:24:17,658 --> 00:24:18,825
Agent Hightower.

462
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:24,456
- You lied to me.
- Detective Reece has some concerns

463
00:24:24,581 --> 00:24:26,208
about the Landon Wale case.

464
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,295
Seems like you didn't tell him
that Jane is the brother-in-law

465
00:24:30,420 --> 00:24:33,173
of Daniel Ruskin
the prime suspect.

466
00:24:33,298 --> 00:24:35,092
At the time of my conversation
with Detective Reece

467
00:24:35,217 --> 00:24:36,593
I didn't know
about the connection.

468
00:24:36,885 --> 00:24:38,679
I apologize for the oversight.

469
00:24:39,805 --> 00:24:43,225
- I'm supposed to buy that?
- No purchase required, detective.

470
00:24:43,475 --> 00:24:45,686
- Where's Jane now?
- No, I don't know where he is.

471
00:24:46,061 --> 00:24:48,105
You don't know where he is?
Okay.

472
00:24:48,939 --> 00:24:50,649
I tell you what,
this is what I'm going to do.

473
00:24:51,608 --> 00:24:53,110
I'm gonna get an arrest warrant

474
00:24:53,402 --> 00:24:55,445
and I'm gonna have
every cop on the street

475
00:24:55,779 --> 00:24:57,114
looking for him and Ruskin.

476
00:24:57,489 --> 00:24:59,116
You need to get control
of your unit, lady.

477
00:24:59,241 --> 00:25:01,660
What you have right here
is slackness.

478
00:25:04,204 --> 00:25:07,165
If Mr. Jane is involved
in obstruction of justice

479
00:25:07,791 --> 00:25:08,834
aiding and abetting

480
00:25:09,584 --> 00:25:10,919
or anything like that

481
00:25:12,129 --> 00:25:13,171
he's yours.

482
00:25:14,506 --> 00:25:15,549
Are we done?

483
00:25:16,466 --> 00:25:18,927
- I guess we are.
- Keep in touch.

484
00:25:29,855 --> 00:25:30,981
Jane's in trouble.

485
00:25:35,694 --> 00:25:36,737
Detective Rigsby.

486
00:25:37,404 --> 00:25:39,364
- You wanted to talk to me?
- It's agent.

487
00:25:39,698 --> 00:25:42,117
Uh, we're reinterviewing a number
of Mr. Wale's associates.

488
00:25:42,242 --> 00:25:44,036
It's just routine.
Let's go to desk, shall we?

489
00:25:45,495 --> 00:25:46,830
You look... different.

490
00:25:47,831 --> 00:25:51,293
Yeah, it's really hot at the office.
The air's broken.

491
00:25:51,626 --> 00:25:52,711
No money to fix it?

492
00:25:54,463 --> 00:25:56,840
We found out that the company was
gonna file for bankruptcy, Heather.

493
00:25:57,215 --> 00:25:59,509
- The place is broke.
-You should really talk to Melanie.

494
00:25:59,843 --> 00:26:01,386
Yeah, but what happened
to the company?

495
00:26:02,596 --> 00:26:03,680
Do you read the news?

496
00:26:04,181 --> 00:26:06,308
- After you.
- Real estate's not doing so well

497
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,560
and Landon made a bad deal
or seven.

498
00:26:09,186 --> 00:26:11,563
He was a cowboy
a win big, lose big.

499
00:26:12,064 --> 00:26:13,440
Please, take a seat.

500
00:26:18,820 --> 00:26:21,531
So how did, uh, Melanie and Concetta
take the bankruptcy news?

501
00:26:21,907 --> 00:26:24,117
They didn't know.
Landon only told me.

502
00:26:24,451 --> 00:26:27,120
I, uh, I keep the books.

503
00:26:30,749 --> 00:26:32,459
So you're looking at them, huh?

504
00:26:33,543 --> 00:26:35,837
We look at every place
at everybody.

505
00:26:36,171 --> 00:26:37,214
Hmm.

506
00:26:37,589 --> 00:26:39,049
"Hmm" meaning what?

507
00:26:39,257 --> 00:26:41,009
No, nothing. It's just...

508
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:44,221
Who knew he'd be worth more
dead than alive?

509
00:26:44,554 --> 00:26:46,264
- You mean life insurance?
- Uh-huh.

510
00:26:55,690 --> 00:26:56,733
Thank you.

511
00:27:03,323 --> 00:27:05,033
Well, this policy's less
than three months old.

512
00:27:05,367 --> 00:27:07,077
- Did Mrs. Wale take it out?
- Connie?

513
00:27:07,828 --> 00:27:11,414
No. She's not the beneficiary.
Melanie is.

514
00:27:11,998 --> 00:27:13,041
The sister.

515
00:27:14,292 --> 00:27:15,335
Well, what's it worth?

516
00:27:15,627 --> 00:27:17,546
$2 million.

517
00:27:19,089 --> 00:27:21,341
If you know where they are
you need to tell me.

518
00:27:21,716 --> 00:27:23,593
Sac PD's got a manhunt going.

519
00:27:24,136 --> 00:27:26,763
Jane and Danny
could get arrested or shot.

520
00:27:27,597 --> 00:27:29,850
They're survivors.
They're gonna do okay.

521
00:27:30,016 --> 00:27:33,103
- Jane will get fired from the CBI.
- Oh, no.

522
00:27:33,353 --> 00:27:35,605
This job is all he has.

523
00:27:36,606 --> 00:27:40,610
If he's arrested they'll take that from him.
I'm his friend. I can help.

524
00:27:42,821 --> 00:27:43,864
Ms. Lisbon

525
00:27:44,990 --> 00:27:47,659
they just took off.
We don't know where they went.

526
00:27:47,951 --> 00:27:48,994
You swear?

527
00:27:49,411 --> 00:27:50,453
I swear.

528
00:28:05,343 --> 00:28:06,386
My sister...

529
00:28:08,013 --> 00:28:09,139
was the only good--

530
00:28:10,015 --> 00:28:11,933
clean honest thing
that I had in my life...

531
00:28:13,101 --> 00:28:14,144
and you ran off with her.

532
00:28:16,146 --> 00:28:18,565
You took her away from me
away from what she knew, so...

533
00:28:19,357 --> 00:28:21,693
You know, yeah.
I've been mad at you.

534
00:28:22,152 --> 00:28:23,195
Very mad.

535
00:28:24,321 --> 00:28:26,198
I didn't--
I didn't take her away.

536
00:28:29,326 --> 00:28:31,578
She didn't--she didn't want
the carny life. She hated it.

537
00:28:31,703 --> 00:28:34,039
She wanted to get out.
We--we both did.

538
00:28:34,873 --> 00:28:36,374
And you know how hard that is.

539
00:28:37,167 --> 00:28:39,252
That was--that was our thing.
That's what we did together.

540
00:28:39,377 --> 00:28:41,671
We--we--we escaped together.

541
00:28:42,130 --> 00:28:43,632
Nice escape plan, bro.

542
00:28:44,174 --> 00:28:46,259
- You got her killed.
- Thanks for reminding me.

543
00:28:46,551 --> 00:28:48,428
Yeah, you just had
to be a big shot

544
00:28:48,720 --> 00:28:51,223
had to get on the TV
and run your mouth.

545
00:28:52,807 --> 00:28:54,267
It's your fault she's dead.

546
00:28:55,602 --> 00:28:57,437
Yes. It is.

547
00:28:58,939 --> 00:29:01,107
I know that.
It is my fault.

548
00:29:02,984 --> 00:29:06,279
And I just-- I hope that one day
you will, uh, forgive me.

549
00:29:07,739 --> 00:29:09,282
And maybe one day
I'll forgive myself.

550
00:29:10,033 --> 00:29:12,827
- Forgive you?
- Not for my sake. For yours.

551
00:29:13,828 --> 00:29:17,457
Because hating me is just a waste
of your energy. It's pointless.

552
00:29:18,833 --> 00:29:21,336
Just move on. Drop it.

553
00:29:21,544 --> 00:29:23,129
Find something to love.

554
00:29:24,047 --> 00:29:25,090
Love?

555
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,885
- Man, you really have changed.
- Yeah.

556
00:29:31,513 --> 00:29:33,682
I don't--
I don't know if I...

557
00:29:34,808 --> 00:29:37,936
I don't require an answer, Danny.
I just...

558
00:29:43,066 --> 00:29:44,317
You got something in your eye?

559
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:47,529
I got allergies. It's...

560
00:29:48,488 --> 00:29:49,614
It's pollen.

561
00:29:51,533 --> 00:29:52,575
Hey.

562
00:29:53,910 --> 00:29:54,953
I'm sorry.

563
00:29:59,499 --> 00:30:00,542
Landon Wale.

564
00:30:05,964 --> 00:30:07,132
Yeah, Landon.

565
00:30:07,841 --> 00:30:08,883
Boy...

566
00:30:09,968 --> 00:30:11,011
There's a mark.

567
00:30:13,972 --> 00:30:16,391
He was so hot to get taken.

568
00:30:16,516 --> 00:30:17,976
He called me that night

569
00:30:18,560 --> 00:30:20,061
and wanted to move up
the action.

570
00:30:21,479 --> 00:30:23,982
When I got there, he was dead.
That's it.

571
00:30:25,650 --> 00:30:27,986
- I did not kill him.
- What was the action?

572
00:30:29,112 --> 00:30:31,656
Landon was supposed to bring me
the gold statue--

573
00:30:32,032 --> 00:30:34,159
not to give to me
just to show me, you know

574
00:30:34,284 --> 00:30:37,120
to prove he had the collateral
to invest in my hedge fund coup.

575
00:30:37,454 --> 00:30:39,414
And this mook
was hooked deep.

576
00:30:39,998 --> 00:30:41,916
Thought he was flying to Brazil
with his hot assistant

577
00:30:42,042 --> 00:30:43,126
and all the money.

578
00:30:43,376 --> 00:30:44,878
Brazil, I like it.

579
00:30:45,503 --> 00:30:46,671
- Old school.
- Yeah.

580
00:30:47,630 --> 00:30:50,967
He had it all mapped out little place
on the beach, a fishing boat.

581
00:30:51,343 --> 00:30:52,385
Perfect mark.

582
00:30:54,262 --> 00:30:57,724
Hey. To suckers. Gotta love 'em.

583
00:31:15,492 --> 00:31:16,534
Don't move.

584
00:31:20,955 --> 00:31:21,998
Keys.

585
00:31:28,797 --> 00:31:29,839
Go on.

586
00:31:41,142 --> 00:31:42,185
Jane!

587
00:31:44,771 --> 00:31:45,814
Jane!

588
00:31:51,027 --> 00:31:52,153
Jane, it's me.

589
00:31:53,071 --> 00:31:54,114
Hey, Lisbon.

590
00:31:55,031 --> 00:31:58,243
- Excellent work finding us.
- I am very unhappy with you.

591
00:31:58,701 --> 00:31:59,994
- Is he in there?
- Yeah.

592
00:32:00,453 --> 00:32:03,373
Bring him out. No funny business
or I will shoot to kill.

593
00:32:04,165 --> 00:32:06,126
You're very persuasive.
We'll be right out.

594
00:32:20,723 --> 00:32:22,016
Ms. Anders, thanks for coming in.

595
00:32:22,183 --> 00:32:23,518
Sure. Uh, what's this about?

596
00:32:23,643 --> 00:32:25,728
Uh, the insurance policy.
We, uh, have a few questions.

597
00:32:25,937 --> 00:32:26,980
Policy?

598
00:32:27,814 --> 00:32:29,566
Oh, for Landon. Sure.

599
00:32:30,233 --> 00:32:31,985
You know, it's common to have
a key man policy

600
00:32:32,110 --> 00:32:33,945
- for small businesses.
- I'm sure you can straighten things out.

601
00:32:34,112 --> 00:32:35,947
We have some, uh, paperwork
to take care of.

602
00:32:38,032 --> 00:32:40,410
If you could heck here
and sign here, please.

603
00:32:45,832 --> 00:32:47,041
Thanks for the call, Agent Lisbon.

604
00:32:47,250 --> 00:32:49,043
My pleasure. We have a deal?

605
00:32:49,210 --> 00:32:51,337
Yeah, we'll forget about
your lies and incompetence.

606
00:32:51,504 --> 00:32:52,547
- All right, up against the car.
- Hey, what!

607
00:32:52,672 --> 00:32:53,715
- Get your hands behind your back.
- Wait. Hey.

608
00:32:53,840 --> 00:32:54,883
- Hands behind the back.
- Hey!

609
00:32:55,008 --> 00:32:56,593
You said we could work it out
if I came in, not him.

610
00:32:56,718 --> 00:32:58,344
- I got no deal with him.
- It's for the best, Danny.

611
00:32:58,470 --> 00:33:00,430
It's for the best. We've all gotta get out
from underneath it sometime.

612
00:33:00,555 --> 00:33:01,848
- You bastard!
- Sorry.

613
00:33:02,765 --> 00:33:06,102
God. You son of a bitch!
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

614
00:33:06,603 --> 00:33:07,687
- How could you do this?
- Take it easy.

615
00:33:07,937 --> 00:33:10,106
I'll kill you! You betrayed me.

616
00:33:12,901 --> 00:33:13,943
I will kill you!

617
00:33:25,205 --> 00:33:27,540
- Did you have to be so rough with him?
- "Don't tell me how to do my job."

618
00:33:27,665 --> 00:33:29,042
- I mean, your bedside--
- "You're lucky I'm not taking you in."

619
00:33:29,209 --> 00:33:30,251
- All right, both of you--
- Are you threatening me?

620
00:33:30,376 --> 00:33:31,419
I'm not threatening anybody.

621
00:33:31,544 --> 00:33:32,587
If it weren't for me
you wouldn't even have him!

622
00:33:32,712 --> 00:33:34,464
Are you delusional?
You blocked the investigation

623
00:33:34,589 --> 00:33:35,632
- You spat on me.
- every step of the way.

624
00:33:35,757 --> 00:33:36,799
- He spat on me!
- That's enough.

625
00:33:36,925 --> 00:33:37,967
- You wanna go in with him? Say the word.
- Enough.

626
00:33:38,092 --> 00:33:39,135
I'd be happy--

627
00:33:40,386 --> 00:33:41,471
"This whole investigation..."

628
00:33:44,182 --> 00:33:47,143
- Hey! Hey, hey! Stop!
- Lisbon! Lisbon!

629
00:33:48,019 --> 00:33:49,062
Hey!

630
00:33:50,063 --> 00:33:52,023
Stop! Hey!

631
00:34:16,629 --> 00:34:18,047
Hi. This is police business.

632
00:34:19,048 --> 00:34:20,841
Patrick Jane. I'm with the CBI.

633
00:34:21,467 --> 00:34:23,135
Yes, I saw you there

634
00:34:23,261 --> 00:34:24,512
- when the killer escaped.
- Yeah.

635
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:27,515
It was horrible, Connie.
Terrible story.

636
00:34:27,807 --> 00:34:29,892
Yeah, well, I'd like to speak
to Ms. Wale alone, please.

637
00:34:30,017 --> 00:34:31,143
It's very important.

638
00:34:33,187 --> 00:34:34,230
Thank you.

639
00:34:53,708 --> 00:34:55,626
This is awkward
but we have reason to believe

640
00:34:55,751 --> 00:34:58,212
that Danny Ruskin has
every intention of killing you.

641
00:34:58,879 --> 00:34:59,922
- Me?
- Yes, you.

642
00:35:00,047 --> 00:35:02,300
He has a violent temper
and several convictions to prove it

643
00:35:02,425 --> 00:35:05,219
including shooting and killing a man
ten years ago.

644
00:35:06,095 --> 00:35:07,680
But why would
he wanna hurt me?

645
00:35:09,515 --> 00:35:10,808
He figured it out.

646
00:35:12,310 --> 00:35:14,687
Oh, I-I'm sorry.
That you killed your own husband

647
00:35:14,812 --> 00:35:17,315
and in doing so
ruined Danny Ruskin's life.

648
00:35:17,940 --> 00:35:18,983
What?

649
00:35:19,191 --> 00:35:21,569
Mr. Jane, that's an outrageous charge.

650
00:35:21,694 --> 00:35:23,863
Yes, one I almost
didn't believe myself

651
00:35:23,988 --> 00:35:25,031
until meeting you just now.

652
00:35:25,156 --> 00:35:28,284
Then it became glaringly obvious
you have deep-seated control issues

653
00:35:28,409 --> 00:35:29,577
mixed in with jealousy

654
00:35:29,702 --> 00:35:32,121
and your own weird lust
for violence.

655
00:35:32,455 --> 00:35:35,166
Landon was gonna take the money
and run away with that leggy assistant.

656
00:35:35,291 --> 00:35:37,918
- What's her name?
- Shut up. Landon loved me.

657
00:35:38,044 --> 00:35:39,420
No, he didn't
and you know he didn't.

658
00:35:39,545 --> 00:35:42,048
Hell, maybe you even knew that he was
headed off to Brazil with her

659
00:35:42,173 --> 00:35:45,676
but what you didn't know, Mrs. Wale
is that Landon was being played.

660
00:35:45,801 --> 00:35:48,638
He was being conned by no one
other than Danny Ruskin.

661
00:35:49,388 --> 00:35:51,474
And when Landon
took your Aphrodite statue

662
00:35:51,932 --> 00:35:54,060
you assumed he was
gonna give it to the mistress.

663
00:35:54,935 --> 00:35:56,228
Your honeymoon gift--

664
00:35:57,688 --> 00:35:59,940
the very symbol
of your love for each other.

665
00:36:01,067 --> 00:36:03,527
"So you followed Landon to where
you thought he was gonna meet"

666
00:36:03,653 --> 00:36:05,279
"with that statuesque strumpet"

667
00:36:05,696 --> 00:36:06,822
"and you killed him."

668
00:36:17,750 --> 00:36:20,169
"Then you took what you thought
was rightfully yours."

669
00:36:23,089 --> 00:36:24,215
That's ridiculous.

670
00:36:24,924 --> 00:36:27,134
That Ruskin character killed Landon.

671
00:36:32,723 --> 00:36:34,809
Where is the statue now, Concetta?

672
00:36:35,893 --> 00:36:36,936
Huh?

673
00:36:38,688 --> 00:36:39,730
Hey, wait!

674
00:36:40,690 --> 00:36:41,732
Wait!

675
00:36:42,358 --> 00:36:43,401
"You can't go in there!"

676
00:36:43,526 --> 00:36:45,444
Oh, look at this. You could land
a jumbo jet in here.

677
00:36:45,945 --> 00:36:47,988
Landon wasn't big
on the, uh, subtlety, was he?

678
00:36:48,114 --> 00:36:50,157
Probably why you knew
he was having an affair.

679
00:36:50,991 --> 00:36:52,827
You must leave, Mr. Jane.

680
00:36:54,662 --> 00:36:55,996
Right now.

681
00:36:56,122 --> 00:36:57,206
You bitch.

682
00:37:00,084 --> 00:37:01,919
- And you.
- Easy.

683
00:37:02,336 --> 00:37:04,755
- Christmas came early this year.
- Oh, Danny, another gun?

684
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,799
Come on. Really?
What--just...

685
00:37:06,924 --> 00:37:08,467
None of this would have happened
except for you.

686
00:37:08,592 --> 00:37:10,594
- You ruined everything.
- Okay, listen. Danny...

687
00:37:11,137 --> 00:37:12,888
- You don't have to do this.
- Shut up!

688
00:37:13,180 --> 00:37:16,600
Okay, listen to me.
You're not this person.

689
00:37:17,017 --> 00:37:19,395
- Okay? You're not this person. Look--
- You backstabbed me!

690
00:37:19,937 --> 00:37:21,063
I trusted you.

691
00:37:21,897 --> 00:37:24,400
You think I'm a mark?
You think you can run games on me?

692
00:37:26,736 --> 00:37:28,237
Oh. Oh, my God.

693
00:37:30,531 --> 00:37:31,907
You shot me, Danny.

694
00:37:33,617 --> 00:37:34,660
Son of a bitch.

695
00:37:36,746 --> 00:37:37,788
What'd you do that for?

696
00:37:37,913 --> 00:37:39,039
- Oh, my God.
- Patrick.

697
00:37:40,541 --> 00:37:41,584
Bastard.

698
00:37:42,668 --> 00:37:43,711
No.

699
00:37:45,171 --> 00:37:46,964
No. No, no, no, no.

700
00:37:51,761 --> 00:37:54,472
Stay with me.
Stay with me. I'm sorry.

701
00:37:54,722 --> 00:37:56,265
I'm sorry.

702
00:38:02,396 --> 00:38:03,439
You made me shoot him.

703
00:38:03,814 --> 00:38:05,399
No, no. No, please.

704
00:38:05,733 --> 00:38:06,984
- This is your fault.
- No.

705
00:38:07,526 --> 00:38:09,612
This is your fault! God!

706
00:38:10,863 --> 00:38:12,323
You ruined my life!

707
00:38:13,032 --> 00:38:14,325
You deserve this, bitch.

708
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:16,160
Your ruined my life.
I could've had everything!

709
00:38:16,285 --> 00:38:17,369
Okay, I can fix it!

710
00:38:18,621 --> 00:38:20,623
I'll fix it. I swear.

711
00:38:22,041 --> 00:38:23,083
Money.

712
00:38:23,292 --> 00:38:26,337
So much money, you can go to Switzerland.
You can go anywhere you want.

713
00:38:26,462 --> 00:38:28,172
- Yeah?
- You don't have to kill me.

714
00:38:29,423 --> 00:38:31,550
Look, I can prove it.

715
00:38:32,092 --> 00:38:33,344
Yeah? Go!

716
00:38:33,677 --> 00:38:35,387
Okay. Okay.

717
00:38:39,099 --> 00:38:40,142
Okay.

718
00:38:41,435 --> 00:38:43,604
This is worth a lot of money.
Take it.

719
00:38:43,813 --> 00:38:45,147
It's yours. Take it!

720
00:38:52,613 --> 00:38:55,741
Connie, Connie, Connie.
You fell for the oldest gag in the book.

721
00:38:56,200 --> 00:38:58,035
Huh?
And one of the cheapest--

722
00:38:58,160 --> 00:39:00,162
$3.55 at a novelty store near you.

723
00:39:00,412 --> 00:39:02,122
Beats the hell outta the cackle bladder.

724
00:39:02,873 --> 00:39:06,085
- You got a little...
- A li--a little...

725
00:39:06,919 --> 00:39:09,004
Kind of minty.
How are my teeth?

726
00:39:09,922 --> 00:39:11,215
They're good?
That was great, huh?

727
00:39:12,842 --> 00:39:14,176
Concetta Wale, you're under arrest.

728
00:39:14,635 --> 00:39:16,178
Turn around. Put your hands
behind your back.

729
00:39:18,013 --> 00:39:19,139
- Turn around.
- I'll take that.

730
00:39:24,228 --> 00:39:25,271
You...

731
00:39:26,438 --> 00:39:27,565
Come on. Let's go.

732
00:39:29,817 --> 00:39:32,695
Sac PD wanna talk to you
about Landon Wale and K-Ram.

733
00:39:32,820 --> 00:39:34,446
There are some
fraud charges pending.

734
00:39:36,240 --> 00:39:38,367
Fraud is very hard to prove

735
00:39:38,492 --> 00:39:40,286
especially when nothing
changed hands.

736
00:39:40,411 --> 00:39:42,538
In fact, now I think of it

737
00:39:43,038 --> 00:39:44,164
I'm actually innocent here.

738
00:39:44,623 --> 00:39:45,958
Whatever. They're on their way.

739
00:39:48,043 --> 00:39:50,671
I believe she's telling you
to scram.

740
00:39:51,630 --> 00:39:52,965
That's not what I said.

741
00:40:05,561 --> 00:40:07,605
- Thank you, Lisbon.
- I didn't hear that.

742
00:40:10,649 --> 00:40:11,734
Thank you, Lisbon.

743
00:40:12,484 --> 00:40:13,694
I can't hear anything.

744
00:40:33,797 --> 00:40:34,840
So...

745
00:40:35,382 --> 00:40:36,425
This is it, huh?

746
00:40:38,135 --> 00:40:39,178
It's nice.

747
00:40:39,720 --> 00:40:40,763
Classy.

748
00:40:42,097 --> 00:40:44,141
They'd like it, I guess

749
00:40:45,017 --> 00:40:46,101
if they had a preference.

750
00:40:48,020 --> 00:40:49,772
You know, this is
the first time I've been here

751
00:40:50,731 --> 00:40:51,774
since the funeral.

752
00:40:55,194 --> 00:40:56,236
Why is that?

753
00:40:58,572 --> 00:40:59,823
Because they're not here.

754
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:10,125
Hey, who knows for sure? Maybe they're up
there right now looking down at us.

755
00:41:11,585 --> 00:41:14,713
You know, Annie's saying
"Lighten up, you dummies."

756
00:41:16,298 --> 00:41:17,424
Yeah, maybe.

757
00:41:21,178 --> 00:41:22,596
I'm sorry I asked to come.

758
00:41:23,222 --> 00:41:26,016
Who knew a trip to the cemetery
would be such a downer?

759
00:41:27,601 --> 00:41:30,020
Sorry. It's irrational.
No reason to be sad.

760
00:41:35,818 --> 00:41:37,945
You gonna give 'em
those flowers or what?

761
00:41:50,624 --> 00:41:51,959
Guilt is for marks.

762
00:41:55,004 --> 00:41:56,130
You know that, right?

763
00:41:57,756 --> 00:41:58,799
Yeah.

